# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EmailJS — contact form delivery (https://www.emailjs.com)
#
# These values are PUBLIC by design (they run in the browser). Copy this file
# to `.env.local` for local dev, and set the SAME three variables in Vercel:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables → (Production + Preview), then redeploy.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create an EmailJS account and add an Email Service (connect the mailbox
#      you want inquiries delivered to, e.g. office@sns-austria.com).
#   2. Create an Email Template. It should reference these variables — they
#      match the contact form's field `name`s exactly:
#        {{name}}     – sender's name
#        {{email}}    – sender's email   (set the template's Reply-To to {{email}})
#        {{phone}}    – sender's phone (may be blank)
#        {{service}}  – type of service selected
#        {{message}}  – the message
#      Set the template's "To" address to office@sns-austria.com.
#   3. Copy the Service ID, Template ID, and Public Key into the vars below.
#   4. In EmailJS, turn on anti-abuse: add reCAPTCHA to the template and/or
#      restrict allowed domains to your site (keys are public, so this matters).
#
# Until these are set, the form gracefully falls back to opening the visitor's
# email client (mailto) so it's never a dead end.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
